resources.string:
1) mathematics (formal);
2) math (US);
3) maths (UK);
4) "used to do sth" means that I did it in the past but now I don't do it anymore;
5) By the way, in this meaning: anymore (US), any more (UK)

1) We use the Past Simple in that dialogue (the 2nd verb form);
2) lie down (phrasal verb);
3) lie - lay - lain (we need this verb in that context);
4) lie - lied - lied; 5) lay - laid - laid.

1) A sheep - four sheep (same form in singular and plural);
2) Scissors are plural, so it should be "these scissors aren't very sharp";
3) Jeans are plural, so we say "a pair of jeans";
4) Police are plural, so the correct question is "Do the police know the cause of the explosion?"

Present Perfect Tense:
1) have/has + V3;
2) have/has + been TO (some place);
3) "Go to the library" -> "have gone to the library" (Present Perfect).
